# Trivy suppressions — read by the `docker` job of CI (aquasecurity/trivy-action reads
# `.trivyignore` from the workspace root). Policy (15_SECURITY.md §9.4):
#
#   * only findings we cannot fix ourselves may be listed here;
#   * every entry states the affected component, why it is not exploitable for Raven and the date
#     it must be re-checked (plain `.trivyignore` holds bare IDs, so the review date is a comment);
#   * anything fixable is fixed in the Dockerfile or the lockfile, never suppressed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# usr/bin/caddy (gobinary) in `caddy:2-alpine`
#
# The static web image serves pre-built assets from /srv over plain HTTP on :8080 behind the
# platform ingress: no DNS resolution of untrusted names, no TLS/ACME client, no XML/ASN.1/MIME
# parsing and no Go html/template rendering happen in that configuration. The CVEs below are in
# the Go standard library and golang.org/x/* linked into the upstream Caddy release binary; they
# can only be cleared by an upstream rebuild against Go >= 1.26.6, so they are suppressed here.
# RE-CHECK BY 2026-10-01: bump `caddy:2-alpine` and delete every line below that Trivy no longer
# reports.
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-39822
CVE-2026-42504
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56852
CVE-2026-56853
# CVE-2026-56854 is in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh (auth bypass via unenforced source-address
# restrictions); the web image's Caddy runs as a static file server and exposes no SSH endpoint.
CVE-2026-56854
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862
# google.golang.org/grpc v1.81.0, also linked into the upstream `caddy:2-alpine` release binary.
# GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf covers the xDS RBAC filter and HTTP/2 handling of gRPC-Go; the web image
# runs Caddy as a static file server with neither gRPC nor xDS enabled, and the fix requires an
# upstream rebuild against grpc-go >= 1.82.1.
# RE-CHECK BY 2026-10-01 together with the CVEs above.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf
